+## Plain-language methodology and uncapped custom multiples — 2026-10-10
+
+- **Change:** Rewrote the methodology with plain definitions of EPS, FCF, P/E and CAGR; explained the 10% business-metric growth benchmark and 0.6 duration weight; checked a worked example. Simplified the growth-card heading and removed the 60× limit from positive finite custom inputs, preserving the automatic cap. Updated guide, README, reference fixtures and public history.
+- **Tests:** The revised 100× cases and new regression reproduced the clipping before the fix. Afterward, all 43 Node and 5 Python tests pass. Production build passes with 6,551 company snapshots and 485 company pages. Exact Markdown exponents, methodology links and example arithmetic are checked. All company data are byte-identical to the prior build.
+- **Browser:** At 1440×900 and 390×844 the methodology and growth label show without document horizontal overflow. Normal numeric keyboard input gives 100.0×; Reset restores 60.0× for Amazon's default window. Browser warning/error logs are empty. Existing CSV serialization uses the same applied-multiple valuation points; a saved browser export was not independently checked in this run.
+- **Maintenance:** PROJECT_LOG, ISSUE-014 and content/updates.json record the behavior/explanation change. The analysis repository's canonical methodology is unchanged, so its project/issue logs do not require entries.
+- **Publication:** Published to https://stockvaluelens.com as Cloudflare version `3d9ef4b0-19e4-4c2b-ab19-7b08070cb742`, uploading 494 changed assets. Eight live HTML/Markdown/script endpoints return HTTP 200 and exactly match the tested build. Live Amazon accepts 100× and Reset restores 60×; the methodology renders the benchmark and partial-weight explanations with no warning/error logs. Screenshots, source patch and release record are preserved in the companion analysis repository.
